  "Delib_end_time": "1:03 p.m.",
  "notes": "Jury polled at plaintiff's request; all jurors confirmed verdict. Judgment entered in favor of Defendant. Plaintiff's Exhibit 953 admitted during pre-jury discussion. Jury verdict filed conventionally per General Order 2007-3."
}

{
  "Final_trial_day": 4,
  "Delib_start_time": "12:59",
  "Delib_end_time": "3:38",
  "notes": "Two Rule 50 motions were denied: one on the general motion and one specifically on the affirmative defense. Trial duration recorded as three hours and 34 minutes. Jury verdict filed conventionally per General Order 2008-03."
}

{
  "Final_trial_day": 11,
  "Delib_start_time": "11:32",
  "Delib_end_time": "3:29 p.m.",
  "notes": "Deliberation start time recorded as '11:32' without 'a.m.' designation. During deliberations at 2:23 p.m. the court convened without jury to discuss and agree on a written answer to a juror question. Exhibits and depositions returned to counsel; original Verdict Form filed conventionally per General Order 2007-03. Total court time recorded as 02:24."
}

{
  "Delib_start_time": "2:54 p.m.",
  "Delib_adjourn_time": "2:55 p.m.",
  "Delib_resume_time": null,
  "notes": "Jury began deliberations at 2:54 p.m. Court went into recess at 2:55 p.m. with trial continued. Jury recessed deliberations at 4:50 p.m. and will resume tomorrow morning at 9:00 a.m. Total time in court was 4 hours, 13 minutes. Two jury questions (5 and 6) were submitted during trial: (5) 'Is it relevant, permissable or helpful for the jury to know the outcome of the Kim case?' and (6) 'How many staff worked on the meat side and how many on the hide side?'"
}

{
  "Delib_start_time": "4:50 p.m.",
  "Delib_adjourn_time": "4:56 p.m.",
  "Delib_resume_time": null,
  "notes": "Jury recessed at 4:52 p.m. and will resume deliberations the following morning at 9:00 a.m. A question from Juror No. 4 regarding a specified jury instruction and evidence was discussed after the jury was excused. CSO was sworn. Deliberations began only briefly on this day before adjournment."
}

{
  "Final_trial_day": 7,
  "Delib_start_time": null,
  "Delib_end_time": "3:54 p.m.",
  "notes": "Jury resumed deliberations at 9:00 a.m. (deliberations started on a prior day). The Court questioned the jury about an unintentional 'question mark' on the Special Verdict Form; the Foreperson circled and initialed the item. Jury was polled, verdict received at 4:10 p.m., jury excused at 4:11 p.m. Time in court was only 8 minutes. Document is an amended courtroom minutes entry."
}

{
  "Final_trial_day": 4,
  "Delib_start_time": "9:41 a.m.",
  "Delib_end_time": "11:58 a.m.",
  "notes": "There was a mid-deliberation recess (11:00 a.m. to 11:58 a.m.) during which the court addressed jurors' questions with parties; Mr. Polin appeared by phone for that session. After verdict was read, court granted plaintiff's oral request for a permanent injunction enjoining the Board of County Commissioners from enforcing its zoning code in a way that would require the sober living house to be removed, subject to submission of a written order. Total court time recorded as 01:06."
}

{
  "Final_trial_day": 6,
  "Delib_start_time": null,
  "Delib_end_time": null,
  "notes": "Case settled before jury deliberations began. Court imposed jury costs of $4,950.76 to be paid equally between plaintiff and defendants. Order Dismissing Case with Prejudice signed. Jury was informed of settlement and discharged. No verdict was reached. Total court time on final day was 16 minutes."
}

{
  "Delib_start_time": null,
  "Delib_adjourn_time": "5:24 p.m.",
  "Delib_resume_time": null,
  "notes": "Deliberations did not actually begin on this day. The jury was sent into recess until Tuesday, August 12, 2014, commencing at 8:30 a.m. (MDT) to commence deliberations. Closing arguments were completed, jury instructions were given, and the jury was adjourned before deliberations began. The court noted it would reconvene August 12, 2014 at approximately 4:45 p.m. (MDT) unless a question or verdict notice was received sooner. Exhibits 42-44, 132, and 177 were excluded from evidence available to the jury. Corrected jury instructions were distributed to jurors and counsel."
}

{
  "Final_trial_day": 7,
  "Delib_start_time": null,
  "Delib_end_time": "11:33 a.m.",
  "notes": "Deliberations had concluded before court convened; court opened at 11:33 a.m. specifically to receive the verdict. Deliberation start time not recorded in this document — likely in a prior day's minutes. Total time in court was only 10 minutes. Jury verdict filed conventionally per General Order 2007-3."
}

{
  "Final_trial_day": 4,
  "Delib_start_time": "10:33 a.m.",
  "Delib_end_time": "2:34 p.m.",
  "notes": "The verdict notification timestamp is recorded as '2:10 a.m.' which is almost certainly a typographical error and should read '2:10 p.m.' given the sequential context of the day's events. Multiple Court Security Officers were sworn in at intervals during deliberations (Gary Osborne at 11:00 a.m., Katherine Maestas at 11:30 a.m., Terry Simmons at 12:30 p.m.). Jurors were polled at the request of the defendant."
}

{
  "Delib_start_time": "1:30 p.m.",
  "Delib_adjourn_time": "4:32 p.m.",
  "Delib_resume_time": null,
  "notes": "Jury submitted a question at 2:40 p.m. during deliberations; court recessed to research the answer and delivered it to the jury at 3:06 p.m. Jury had not reached a verdict by end of day and was excused until 9:00 a.m. on May 22, 2015. Court also advised jury of Rule 50 rulings dismissing Defendant Ensminger and finding Defendants Weatherill's and Hartbauer's violation of Plaintiff's 4th Amendment rights before deliberations began."
}

{
  "Final_trial_day": 5,
  "Delib_start_time": null,
  "Delib_end_time": "11:42 a.m.",
  "notes": "Deliberations began at 9:00 a.m. on this final day (Day 5) per the minutes narrative, but no formal timestamp entry marks that start — it is described in prose only. The jury had reconvened from a prior day. Verdict was in favor of plaintiff and against all defendants. Counsel declined jury poll. Total session time was 11 minutes."
}

{
  "Final_trial_day": 7,
  "Delib_start_time": "9:00 a.m.",
  "Delib_end_time": "4:26 p.m.",
  "notes": "Jury sent two questions during deliberations (at 2:45 p.m. and 3:59 p.m.). Court responded in writing to the first question and read jury instruction 28 aloud for the second. Jury was briefly brought into courtroom at 4:10 p.m. for the second question response before resuming deliberations. Verdict reached and read at 4:30 p.m.; jury polled at 4:31 p.m. and discharged at 4:35 p.m. Defendant's Motion to Strike Plaintiff's Expert Economist (ECF Doc. No. 153) denied as moot. Exhibits returned to counsel at conclusion of trial. Total court time recorded as 31 minutes."
}

{
  "Final_trial_day": 5,
  "Delib_start_time": "11:56 a.m.",
  "Delib_end_time": "2:00 p.m.",
  "notes": "Jury sent a note to chambers at 12:55 p.m. during deliberations; court reconvened at 1:30 p.m. to discuss the note, then recessed again at 1:46 p.m. before reconvening at 2:00 p.m. when the verdict was received. Plaintiff requested jury poll; all jurors affirmed the verdict. Total in-court time was 3 hours, 24 minutes."
}

{
  "Final_trial_day": 10,
  "Delib_start_time": "12:18 p.m.",
  "Delib_end_time": "5:23 p.m.",
  "notes": "Jury requested additional deliberation time; court granted an extra 30 minutes. Verdict was unanimous. Defendant ordered to file motion for attorneys' fees and costs by October 14, 2016. Total time in court recorded as 3:54. Exhibits and depositions returned to counsel at conclusion of trial."
}
